---
import LegalLayout from '../layouts/LegalLayout.astro';
import { site } from '../data/site.js';

const updated = '22 August 2026';
---

<LegalLayout title="Terms of Service" updated={updated}>
  <p>
    These terms govern your use of <strong>ekstechub.com</strong>. They are not the terms
    of any engagement — paid work is governed by the separate written agreement we sign
    with you, and where the two differ, that agreement wins.
  </p>

  <h2>Using this site</h2>
  <p>
    You may read, print and share the content of this site for your own use. You may not
    copy it to present our work as your own, scrape it at a scale that degrades service
    for others, or attempt to interfere with the site's operation. The content, layout and
    branding remain the property of {site.name}.
  </p>

  <h2>What this site is and is not</h2>
  <p>
    Everything here is general information about the services we offer. It is not a quote,
    an offer, or professional advice for your particular situation. Descriptions of our
    services, timelines and processes are indicative and may change.
  </p>
  <p>
    Submitting the contact form does not create a contract or oblige us to take on your
    work, and it does not oblige you to engage us. An engagement begins only when both
    sides have agreed a written scope and fee.
  </p>

  <h2>Professional and regulated advice</h2>
  <p>
    <strong>Engineering.</strong> Designs, calculations and recommendations published here
    are illustrative. Nothing on this site should be relied on as a structural, electrical
    or mechanical design for a specific site. Any design we issue for construction is
    identified as such, issued under an engagement, and carries its own assumptions and
    limitations.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>Finance and management.</strong> {site.name} operates as a management and
    financial consultancy. We do not hold client funds, sell financial products, or act as
    a licensed investment advisor, broker or dealer. Nothing on this site is investment,
    tax or legal advice, or a recommendation to buy or sell any financial product. Where a
    matter requires regulated advice, we will say so and refer you to an appropriately
    licensed professional.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>Real estate.</strong> Property information is provided in good faith and
    verified as described on the relevant pages, but availability, pricing and title status
    can change. Verify all particulars independently before committing funds.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>Academic services.</strong> We supervise, review and assess student work. We do
    not write, sit or submit academic work on a student's behalf, and we will not accept an
    engagement to do so. Students remain responsible for complying with their institution's
    academic integrity rules.
  </p>

  <h2>Third-party links and services</h2>
  <p>
    This site links to third-party services, including WhatsApp and our form provider. We
    are not responsible for their content, availability or practices, and your use of them
    is subject to their own terms.
  </p>

  <h2>Liability</h2>
  <p>
    We take care to keep this site accurate, but we do not warrant that it is complete,
    current or uninterrupted. To the fullest extent permitted by law, {site.name} is not
    liable for loss arising from reliance on the general information published here. This
    does not limit liability for death or personal injury caused by negligence, for fraud,
    or for anything else that cannot lawfully be excluded. Liability arising from actual
    engagements is dealt with in the engagement agreement.
  </p>

  <h2>Changes</h2>
  <p>
    We may update these terms. The date at the top of this page shows when they last
    changed, and continued use of the site means you accept the current version.
  </p>

  <h2>Governing law</h2>
  <p>
    These terms are governed by the laws of the Republic of Cameroon, and the courts of
    Cameroon have exclusive jurisdiction over any dispute arising from them.
  </p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>
    Questions about these terms go to
    <a href={`mailto:${site.contact.email}`} class="underline">{site.contact.email}</a>,
    or {site.contact.address}, {site.contact.region}.
  </p>

  <p class="text-sm border-t border-outline-variant pt-6 mt-10">
    <strong>Note for the site owner:</strong> this is a working draft, not legal advice.
    The regulated-advice wording under Finance matters most — have a Cameroonian lawyer
    confirm it reflects your actual licensing position before launch.
  </p>
</LegalLayout>
